# SDK Hooks

Files in `src/main/java/com/cloudinary/account/provisioning/hooks/` are NOT regenerated by Speakeasy (except `SDKHooks.java` is generated once) — custom files are safe to edit.

## Custom files

- `SDKHooks.java` — hook registration, only generated once
- `CloudinaryAccountHook.java` — SdkInit + BeforeRequest (Basic auth + account_id)
- `AccountConfig.java` — env var parsing (CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL + individual vars)
- `UserAgentHook.java` — custom user-agent header (BeforeRequest)

## User-Agent Format

Pattern: `Cloudinary/AccountProvisioning Java/{sdkVersion} Gen/{genVersion} Schema/{schemaVersion} (Java {javaVersion}; {os} {arch})`

## AccountConfig (CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL)

`AccountConfig.java` parses `CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL` with format: `account://<api_key>:<api_secret>@<account_id>`

Individual env vars (`CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDINARY_PROVISIONING_API_KEY`, `CLOUDINARY_PROVISIONING_API_SECRET`) override URL-parsed values.

## Hook lifecycle

1. `sdkInit` — fills `account_id` global path param from env/URL if not explicitly provided
2. `beforeRequest` — resolves credentials from explicit Security or env config, sets Basic Auth header; replaces user-agent header
